1
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:41,480
Think about where to go tomorrow.

2
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:43,120
The Summer Palace and the Temple of Heaven.

3
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:44,599
Which do you think is more fun?

4
00:01:44,599 --> 00:01:45,400
Boss,

5
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:48,680
did you hire me just to be your tour guide?

6
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:50,599
You even got me a pager.

7
00:01:50,599 --> 00:01:51,760
Honestly, with what you're paying,

8
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:53,040
you could easily hire someone

9
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:54,840
much more capable than me.

10
00:01:55,359 --> 00:01:56,680
There are many types of secretaries.

11
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:58,079
You're the most naive one.

12
00:01:58,519 --> 00:02:00,400
There's no such thing as a free meal.

13
00:02:00,879 --> 00:02:02,200
It's just not time to work yet.

14
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:02,879
What's the rush?

15
00:02:11,039 --> 00:02:11,560
Come on.

16
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:14,080
If you're going to copy someone, pick an expert.

17
00:02:14,479 --> 00:02:15,759
The guy in the red hat is an out-of-towner.

18
00:02:15,759 --> 00:02:16,800
Why are you watching him?

19
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:18,039
No,

20
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:20,159
I watched the people downstairs earlier,

21
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:21,280
they all mix it like this.

22
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:24,280
Brother Qi, why don't you try it first?

23
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:38,000
Do you sell salt for a living?

24
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:38,800
It's salty as hell.

25
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:39,759
No, it's...

26
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:41,639
I think this sauce is just like this.

27
00:02:47,639 --> 00:02:48,599
When we get back,

28
00:02:48,599 --> 00:02:49,560
come with me to look at cars.

29
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,400
You're pretty sharp, aren't you?

30
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:52,280
Shop around and

31
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:53,360
find the cheapest car dealership

32
00:02:54,039 --> 00:02:56,000
in Minzhong for me.

33
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,240
Leave this to me.

34
00:02:57,599 --> 00:02:59,120
What kind of car do you want?

35
00:02:59,919 --> 00:03:00,840
Do you need a driver?

36
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:02,840
You know how to drive?

37
00:03:03,439 --> 00:03:04,599
I don't.

38
00:03:04,879 --> 00:03:06,000
My boyfriend does.

39
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,120
Are you kidding me?

40
00:03:08,039 --> 00:03:10,080
A guy who pawned my watch?

41
00:03:10,319 --> 00:03:11,800
Would he sell me out too?

42
00:03:14,639 --> 00:03:15,879
I'll vouch for him.

43
00:03:15,879 --> 00:03:17,280
He definitely won't do it again.

44
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,919
He wouldn't dare break the law.

45
00:03:18,919 --> 00:03:19,879
Whether he'd dare to or not

46
00:03:20,639 --> 00:03:22,719
sometimes depends not only on the cost,

47
00:03:22,719 --> 00:03:24,319
but also on how high the stakes are.

48
00:03:26,319 --> 00:03:27,919
Wipe the sauce off your mouth.

49
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,520
I'm talking about doing business.

50
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:33,919
Do you know what the most profitable business is now?

51
00:03:35,719 --> 00:03:36,639
Military assets.

52
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:40,360
I'm not even talking about selling guns and bullets.

53
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:41,400
Just things like

54
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:42,800
socks, pants,

55
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:43,800
and work gloves.

56
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:45,840
Even tiny things can make a fortune.

57
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:47,680
Introduce me to your aunt.

58
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:49,080
Let's get rich together.

59
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:58,319
If I say no,

60
00:03:59,199 --> 00:04:00,280
are you

61
00:04:00,599 --> 00:04:01,759
going to fire me?

62
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:03,919
It's not impossible.

63
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:12,039
My aunt specifically said

64
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:16,000
not to discuss anything with outsiders lately.

65
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,360
They had a meeting.

66
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:18,759
Whoever talks gets in trouble.

67
00:04:19,199 --> 00:04:19,800
Understood.

68
00:04:20,399 --> 00:04:21,920
You have to zip your lips.

69
00:04:27,879 --> 00:04:30,240
Xiaolu, he

70
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:32,079
also has many friends in the military.

71
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:33,480
And they know about military assets.

72
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:34,240
They're not local,

73
00:04:35,319 --> 00:04:36,199
so there's no need for secrecy.

74
00:04:36,839 --> 00:04:38,079
How's his driving?

75
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:39,600
Will he drive us into a ditch?

76
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:41,360
He used to drive for the government.

77
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:42,800
He won awards every year.

78
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:43,680
You won't find

79
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:45,360
a driver with better skills than him.

80
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:46,759
U-turns, going through tunnels,

81
00:04:46,759 --> 00:04:47,759
and perfect parking...

82
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:49,199
he's an expert at everything.

83
00:04:52,839 --> 00:04:53,879
His bonus will be the same as yours.

84
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:55,720
His salary will be slightly lower.

85
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:56,480
Deal?

86
00:04:57,720 --> 00:04:59,639
We'll do whatever you say.

87
00:04:59,839 --> 00:05:01,800
Boss, a toast to you.

88
00:05:02,959 --> 00:05:03,879
Thank you, Boss.

89
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:33,600
What's that noise upstairs?

90
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:35,959
He's already asleep.

91
00:05:35,959 --> 00:05:37,120
He's even started snoring.

92
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:44,720
Here, have some tea.

93
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:53,759
Why was the sauce at the hot pot place so salty?

94
00:05:54,199 --> 00:05:56,120
I bet yours wasn't salty at all.

95
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:01,639
They all say you're honest,

96
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:02,920
but you're actually the worst.

97
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:03,560
Silently taking revenge.

98
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:04,560
Petty and vindictive.

99
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:05,600
I made you hold your pee,

100
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:06,600
so you put salt in my sauce.

101
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:08,279
Just to make me pour you tea.

102
00:06:08,639 --> 00:06:09,680
I wouldn't dare.

103
00:06:10,959 --> 00:06:12,319
If I couldn't even figure that out,

104
00:06:12,319 --> 00:06:13,319
I might as well quit State Security.

105
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,560
Then what else did you figure out?

106
00:06:18,079 --> 00:06:18,959
You like Jinlan.

107
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:20,959
Not in the slightest.

108
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,040
There are many ways to like someone.

109
00:06:23,839 --> 00:06:25,079
Saying one thing but meaning another is one.

110
00:06:26,639 --> 00:06:29,639
How do you fall asleep and wake up on command?

111
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:31,720
I think that beats tailing and wiretapping.

112
00:06:33,079 --> 00:06:34,600
Being with you is really boring.

113
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:35,680
What else can I do but sleep?

114
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:37,040
Remember this.

115
00:06:37,279 --> 00:06:39,079
In the future, especially during surveillance,

116
00:06:39,959 --> 00:06:41,920
you must find someone interesting.

117
00:06:42,839 --> 00:06:44,319
If you're boring yourself,

118
00:06:44,319 --> 00:06:45,879
you need to find someone who tells jokes.

119
00:06:47,199 --> 00:06:47,920
I get it.

120
00:06:48,759 --> 00:06:49,439
Get what?

121
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:50,959
A partner is very important.

122
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:53,199
Partners, my ass.

123
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:57,360
Life is like this tea.

124
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:58,240
It's too bitter.

125
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:00,639
You have to learn to find your own fun.

126
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:02,560
Otherwise, how do you keep going?

127
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:40,560
Who ran these simulations?

128
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:42,480
These are the Americans' projections.

129
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,199
Do any of you know

130
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:47,079
how long it would take the PLA to land?

131
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:49,639
How long until they reach this very conference room?

132
00:07:49,639 --> 00:07:50,680
How long?

133
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:53,639
Where are the guys from the "MIB"?

134
00:07:53,959 --> 00:07:55,319
They're verifying the intelligence.

135
00:07:55,319 --> 00:07:56,360
They'll be here shortly.

136
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:58,040
So many of us are waiting on them.

137
00:07:58,360 --> 00:07:59,480
We're running out of time.

138
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:01,040
What's taking them so long?

139
00:08:01,199 --> 00:08:02,360
Go hurry them up!

140
00:08:02,439 --> 00:08:03,199
Yes, sir.

141
00:08:03,199 --> 00:08:04,079
I'll get right on it.

142
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:08,879
In recent years,

143
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:12,639
across all fronts of our nation's military technology sector,

144
00:08:12,639 --> 00:08:16,199
numerous role models have emerged.

145
00:08:16,319 --> 00:08:17,360
Today,

146
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:19,519
the Comrades being commended

147
00:08:19,879 --> 00:08:21,879
are the outstanding representatives of this.

148
00:08:21,879 --> 00:08:23,959
Throughout the lives of everyone sitting here,

149
00:08:23,959 --> 00:08:27,639
we have been working for the development and security of our motherland,

150
00:08:27,639 --> 00:08:29,279
making silent contributions.

151
00:08:29,279 --> 00:08:30,680
Especially recently,

152
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:32,960
regarding missile fuel technology,

153
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:34,840
those who have made significant breakthroughs,

154
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:36,799
the Comrades from Institute 761.

155
00:08:36,799 --> 00:08:40,519
You have delved deep and bravely made breakthroughs.

156
00:08:40,519 --> 00:08:42,480
With firm conviction

157
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:44,399
and relentless effort,

158
00:08:44,399 --> 00:08:46,840
for China's defense industry,

159
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:48,960
you are composing a magnificent chapter.

160
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:57,080
I know who the snitch is.

161
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:58,279
Someone familiar?

162
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:01,679
It's not like this hasn't happened before.

163
00:09:01,679 --> 00:09:03,519
It barely made a ripple.

164
00:09:03,519 --> 00:09:05,399
Those due for a promotion still got it.

165
00:09:05,759 --> 00:09:07,440
Did they really pull the list?

166
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:10,440
What's our department thinking?

167
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,639
Maybe we just put it on hold for now.

168
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:15,759
You're still young anyway,

169
00:09:15,919 --> 00:09:16,960
and you have the credentials.

170
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:18,679
A year sooner or later won't matter much.

171
00:10:04,519 --> 00:10:05,279
Who is it?

172
00:10:05,879 --> 00:10:06,519
Engineer Cao.

173
00:10:07,039 --> 00:10:08,440
The director is personally treating us.

174
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:09,759
He's taking everyone to Quanjude.

175
00:10:09,759 --> 00:10:10,639
In ten minutes,

176
00:10:10,639 --> 00:10:11,440
gather on the first floor.

177
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:13,720
I have an upset stomach.

178
00:10:14,279 --> 00:10:14,919
I think I'll pass.

179
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:16,840
I'll go tell the director then.

180
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:17,399
Okay.

181
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:26,720
Didn't I just say

182
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:27,080
I...

183
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:28,519
Mr. Cao, your coffee.

184
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:31,399
I didn't order coffee.

185
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:32,840
Maybe your friend

186
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:34,399
or a colleague ordered it for you.

187
00:10:37,919 --> 00:10:38,840
Thank you.

188
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:39,639
You're welcome.

189
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:46,320
Who's not going?

190
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:47,440
Everyone has to go.

191
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:48,000
Okay.

192
00:10:48,159 --> 00:10:48,759
I'll go, I'll go.

193
00:10:48,759 --> 00:10:49,279
I'll go.

194
00:10:49,279 --> 00:10:50,480
I'll head down as soon as I'm dressed.

195
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:51,120
Hurry up.

196
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:51,639
Everyone's waiting for you.

197
00:10:51,639 --> 00:10:52,320
Okay, okay.

198
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:53,120
You guys head down first.

199
00:11:43,279 --> 00:11:44,279
Beijing Exhibition Center

200
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:44,879
Okay.

201
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:00,080
Sorry about that.

202
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:01,840
Are you alright?

203
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:15,039
Regarding travel reimbursement,

204
00:12:15,039 --> 00:12:16,159
are there specific rules?

205
00:12:16,919 --> 00:12:17,639
What do you mean?

206
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:20,840
I saw you choosing a taxi earlier.

207
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:22,799
Is there a difference between 1.20 and 1.40?

208
00:12:22,799 --> 00:12:23,320
Obviously.

209
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:24,840
This is a Comrade's car.

210
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:31,200
This Erguotou,

211
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:32,960
is 56 percent ABV.

212
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:34,600
Thanks.

213
00:12:35,879 --> 00:12:37,759
When we first came to Beijing for college,

214
00:12:38,759 --> 00:12:40,080
everyone was from the north.

215
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:41,960
Old Jia and I were the only southerners.

216
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:44,759
Our class monitor was a Beijing local.

217
00:12:44,759 --> 00:12:47,240
He forced us to drink Douzhi with him.

218
00:12:47,679 --> 00:12:48,480
Oh, my god.

219
00:12:48,480 --> 00:12:49,279
After just one sip,

220
00:12:49,279 --> 00:12:51,200
I almost threw up on his shoes!

221
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:53,320
After drinking the Douzhi,

222
00:12:53,879 --> 00:12:55,399
he took us to a public bathhouse.

223
00:12:55,399 --> 00:12:57,519
Us southerners had never seen a body scrub before!

224
00:12:57,840 --> 00:12:59,919
In a pool bigger than this private room,

225
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:01,840
there were tall, short, fat, and skinny guys,

226
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:02,960
all completely butt naked.

227
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:04,720
It was embarrassing as hell!

228
00:13:04,879 --> 00:13:06,519
The funniest part was Old Jia.

229
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:08,919
He is extremely nearsighted,

230
00:13:08,919 --> 00:13:10,759
so he went into the bathhouse wearing his glasses.

231
00:13:10,759 --> 00:13:12,720
The lenses got completely fogged up.

232
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:14,679
When he wiped them clean and saw clearly,

233
00:13:15,080 --> 00:13:17,120
he was scared silly.

234
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:18,559
He turned around and ran.

235
00:13:18,559 --> 00:13:20,279
When he got to the door, he realized

236
00:13:20,279 --> 00:13:21,159
he couldn't run any further.

237
00:13:21,159 --> 00:13:21,840
If he kept running,

238
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:23,559
he'd be running onto the street butt naked!

239
00:13:24,279 --> 00:13:26,320
We laughed so hard!

240
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:28,000
Come, come.

241
00:13:29,639 --> 00:13:31,320
Mr. Jiao is here to toast everyone!

242
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:33,279
I heard you all before I even walked in,

243
00:13:33,279 --> 00:13:34,519
cheering louder and louder.

244
00:13:34,879 --> 00:13:35,639
How much have you had?

245
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,639
You're drinking faster than our table!

246
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:38,840
Colleagues,

247
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:41,440
today is a great day for us.

248
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:42,759
On behalf of Institute 761

249
00:13:42,759 --> 00:13:43,720
and the Party Secretary,

250
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:44,480
I'd like to toast you all.

251
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:45,840
Come on, cheers!

252
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:47,320
Thank you, sir.

253
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:48,159
Please, drink up.

254
00:13:48,159 --> 00:13:49,320
Thank you, sir. Thank you, sir.

255
00:13:52,039 --> 00:13:52,879
Engineer Jia,

256
00:13:53,039 --> 00:13:55,480
are we going to a bathhouse after these drinks?

257
00:13:56,799 --> 00:13:57,519
I'll go if he goes.

258
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:01,759
Mr. Jiao is coming to toast again.

259
00:14:04,039 --> 00:14:06,000
I actually need to talk to you about something.

260
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,320
I might need to delay my return by a day.

261
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:10,720
Can you help me change my flight ticket?

262
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:12,120
This needs to be reported in advance.

263
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:13,639
I am telling you before boarding.

264
00:14:13,639 --> 00:14:15,639
Isn't telling you now considered "in advance"?

265
00:14:15,639 --> 00:14:17,679
We really can't just change it on a whim.

266
00:14:17,679 --> 00:14:18,720
The boss set the schedule.

267
00:14:19,919 --> 00:14:21,320
Well, the boss is right here.

268
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:23,200
Just go tell him and it's settled.

269
00:14:23,399 --> 00:14:24,600
I'll pay for the ticket myself.

270
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:25,519
Out of my own pocket.

271
00:14:25,519 --> 00:14:26,440
So I can change it, right?

272
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:29,679
This person is too sensitive.

273
00:14:29,679 --> 00:14:30,840
I'll go handle him.

274
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:32,840
Let me, let me, let me.

275
00:14:33,519 --> 00:14:36,279
Liaoping, have you lost your mind?

276
00:14:36,279 --> 00:14:37,919
The boss was just here

277
00:14:37,919 --> 00:14:39,279
and specifically emphasized

278
00:14:39,279 --> 00:14:41,639
that we must stay together as a group.

279
00:14:41,639 --> 00:14:42,600
And why is that?

280
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:43,919
For confidentiality.

281
00:14:43,919 --> 00:14:45,879
Nobody is singling you out.

282
00:14:45,879 --> 00:14:47,480
Why are you getting so agitated?

283
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:48,480
Let me explain it to you nicely.

284
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:49,519
Explain what?

285
00:14:51,399 --> 00:14:53,000
What, are you going to report me?

286
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:55,679
Bring me down,

287
00:14:56,559 --> 00:14:58,159
so you think you can take my place?

288
00:14:58,440 --> 00:14:59,240
Is that it?

289
00:15:00,879 --> 00:15:04,120
Wipe the dirt off your own face first before you talk.

290
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:41,200
Boss, there are so many foreigners.

291
00:16:00,919 --> 00:16:01,600
Brother Qi.

292
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:04,279
Who do you think he's here to meet?

293
00:16:06,679 --> 00:16:07,720
I have a hunch.

294
00:16:08,559 --> 00:16:09,799
He's not here to make contact.

295
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:11,879
It's a smokescreen.

296
00:16:12,679 --> 00:16:13,519
A smokescreen?

297
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:15,120
To fool who?

298
00:16:24,639 --> 00:16:25,279
Sis Li.

299
00:16:25,279 --> 00:16:26,240
Why is he back here again?

300
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:27,320
Let's wait and see.

301
00:17:22,359 --> 00:17:22,920
Hello.

302
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:23,440
Hi.

303
00:17:23,559 --> 00:17:24,720
I'll have a coffee with extra sugar.

304
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:25,880
Okay. Will you be sitting...

305
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:26,799
I'll be sitting over there.

306
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:27,880
Alright, please wait a moment.

307
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:28,920
I'll bring it over to you shortly.

308
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:29,599
Thank you.

309
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:01,039
Confucius said, "A man without trust,

310
00:18:01,039 --> 00:18:02,079
I know not what he can accomplish."

311
00:18:02,119 --> 00:18:02,960
I'm here.

312
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:04,359
You're heading back tomorrow.

313
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:06,519
If I were your colleague,

314
00:18:06,519 --> 00:18:08,480
I'd also go out to buy some souvenirs,

315
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:10,839
and enjoy the coffee here.

316
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:12,720
There's a jacket on the counter.

317
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:15,279
The size should fit you perfectly.

318
00:18:15,279 --> 00:18:16,160
Do you see it?

319
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:17,839
Okay, okay.

320
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:21,319
Your coffee, sir.

321
00:18:21,759 --> 00:18:22,279
Thank you.

322
00:18:22,839 --> 00:18:23,559
Xiao Wang,

323
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:24,640
you keep watch here.

324
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:26,119
I'll go in and take a look.

325
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:02,119
Boss.

326
00:19:02,559 --> 00:19:03,759
What can I do?

327
00:19:04,079 --> 00:19:05,440
However many people are here,

328
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:07,119
exchange business cards with every one of them.

329
00:19:07,319 --> 00:19:08,839
Do what you do best.

330
00:19:09,119 --> 00:19:09,759
Okay.

331
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:18,079
Sorry. Are you okay?

332
00:19:18,079 --> 00:19:19,119
I'm fine, I'm fine.

333
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:40,240
Once in Beijing, let's not meet again.

334
00:19:40,240 --> 00:19:42,359
You need to be a moving target.

335
00:19:43,319 --> 00:19:44,359
If there's a mantis,

336
00:19:44,359 --> 00:19:46,200
let them focus on you, the cicada.

337
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:47,799
An innocent cicada.

338
00:19:51,759 --> 00:19:53,200
If I play the cicada,

339
00:19:53,720 --> 00:19:54,759
what will the mantis think?

340
00:19:55,519 --> 00:19:57,039
How will he know if I'm clean or not?

341
00:19:57,319 --> 00:19:58,480
I mean, what if...

342
00:19:58,480 --> 00:19:59,319
That won't happen.

343
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:01,319
You just need to tell yourself

344
00:20:01,799 --> 00:20:03,599
that you're a tourist on a business trip.

345
00:20:03,839 --> 00:20:05,119
Just act natural.

346
00:20:05,319 --> 00:20:06,559
Go sightseeing and shopping,

347
00:20:07,200 --> 00:20:08,400
make friends, and do business.

348
00:20:12,160 --> 00:20:13,319
Why are you everywhere?

349
00:20:13,319 --> 00:20:14,319
What a coincidence!

350
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:16,119
When did you arrive?

351
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:17,359
Was it the same day as me?

352
00:20:17,359 --> 00:20:18,119
Right?

353
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:20,039
What day was that, Boss Lin?

354
00:20:20,160 --> 00:20:20,759
Mr. Ma.

355
00:20:22,079 --> 00:20:22,720
Let's go.

356
00:20:23,119 --> 00:20:24,759
You're always where the leaders are.

357
00:20:24,759 --> 00:20:26,279
You shouldn't be in business.

358
00:20:26,279 --> 00:20:27,319
You should be in politics.

359
00:20:28,400 --> 00:20:30,039
His brother-in-law taught him all that.

360
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:32,079
A leader is like a tree.

361
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:34,799
Fruits just keep dropping from this tree.

362
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,240
Aren't you gonna catch them?

363
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:37,440
Our pockets are too small.

364
00:20:37,519 --> 00:20:38,839
They're too big to catch.

365
00:20:39,039 --> 00:20:40,559
And we wouldn't dare compete with you.

366
00:20:40,559 --> 00:20:41,640
Just dealing with medical equipment

367
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:43,160
is enough to feed the two of us.

368
00:20:43,440 --> 00:20:43,799
Computed tomography scanners,

369
00:20:43,799 --> 00:20:45,039
MRI scanners.

370
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:46,920
Aren't there enough in Minzhong?

371
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:48,119
You had to come all the way to Beijing.

372
00:20:48,119 --> 00:20:49,759
And you claim your appetite isn't big.

373
00:20:52,559 --> 00:20:53,559
Your boss...

374
00:20:53,559 --> 00:20:55,000
never tells the truth.

375
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:55,960
So sly.

376
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,920
You promised me a slice of the pie.

377
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,200
What are you guys really up to?

378
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:00,920
You tell me.

379
00:21:01,759 --> 00:21:02,920
Medical equipment leasing.

380
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:04,319
What Brother Qi mentioned...

381
00:21:04,319 --> 00:21:05,079
Like what?

382
00:21:08,599 --> 00:21:09,279
Mr. Ma,

383
00:21:09,799 --> 00:21:12,160
what you said last time at Hope Primary School...

384
00:21:12,279 --> 00:21:13,920
you weren't bluffing, were you?

385
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:17,640
If you want to cooperate, you've got to show your hand.

386
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:36,119
379 Military Hospital.

387
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:39,640
Even hospitals have to balance their books.

388
00:21:39,640 --> 00:21:40,640
Trade-ins.

389
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:41,599
As long as it pays off.

390
00:21:47,599 --> 00:21:49,160
An approval from the Health Bureau.

391
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:50,440
One from Beijing works.

392
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:52,119
Would one from Minzhong work?

393
00:21:56,759 --> 00:21:57,920
Anywhere works.

394
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:01,400
Alright.

395
00:22:01,839 --> 00:22:02,440
Mr. Ma.

396
00:22:02,880 --> 00:22:04,319
I know you're not short on money.

397
00:22:04,319 --> 00:22:06,759
Are you operating collectively or as decentralized franchises?

398
00:22:07,119 --> 00:22:08,240
For an operation this size,

399
00:22:08,920 --> 00:22:10,240
I might not be good at much else,

400
00:22:10,599 --> 00:22:13,039
but I definitely have practical experience with franchises.

401
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:15,720
Let's have a good chat when we get back.

402
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:16,440
Sounds good.

403
00:22:16,440 --> 00:22:17,200
When are you heading back?

404
00:22:17,200 --> 00:22:18,400
As soon as I'm done here.

405
00:22:33,440 --> 00:22:34,440
How many tickets?

406
00:22:34,440 --> 00:22:35,119
One.

407
00:22:37,559 --> 00:22:38,839
I'm alone too.

408
00:22:40,039 --> 00:22:41,279
Why don't we share a rental?

409
00:22:53,839 --> 00:22:55,599
Beijing is even drier than I imagined.

410
00:22:56,640 --> 00:22:57,559
I've got phlegm in my throat.

411
00:22:58,039 --> 00:22:59,599
And I get nosebleeds at night.

412
00:23:00,599 --> 00:23:01,720
It's like that for everyone at first.

413
00:23:02,119 --> 00:23:03,440
You'll be fine in a couple of days.

414
00:23:03,799 --> 00:23:05,440
Choosing a place like this to meet

415
00:23:06,359 --> 00:23:07,720
for a VIP like you,

416
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:09,799
although it's for security reasons,

417
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:13,759
still feels a bit disrespectful.

418
00:23:14,319 --> 00:23:15,240
To be honest,

419
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,559
I didn't expect you to come.

420
00:23:19,960 --> 00:23:21,440
Nor did I think you'd dare to.

421
00:23:21,559 --> 00:23:22,960
I said we'd meet in person,

422
00:23:23,359 --> 00:23:24,640
so we meet in person.

423
00:23:24,960 --> 00:23:26,759
Even if I get caught,

424
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:27,759
or executed,

425
00:23:28,319 --> 00:23:29,799
even if I die in Beijing,

426
00:23:30,559 --> 00:23:32,559
my time in this business wouldn't be in vain.

427
00:23:32,880 --> 00:23:34,880
Missile deployment is like a tree.

428
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:36,480
I can only give you one branch,

429
00:23:37,799 --> 00:23:39,640
the thickest and most crucial one.

430
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:42,119
As for how the rest of the tree grows,

431
00:23:42,359 --> 00:23:44,559
you'll have to piece it together yourselves.

432
00:23:45,119 --> 00:23:46,519
We deal with theoretical research.

433
00:23:52,119 --> 00:23:53,480
Based on my personal speculation,

434
00:23:53,720 --> 00:23:55,839
our technology is quite mature.

435
00:23:56,279 --> 00:23:58,519
But a full upgrade will still take time.

436
00:23:58,759 --> 00:24:00,799
It hasn't reached the set combat parameters.

437
00:24:04,720 --> 00:24:05,960
Let me translate that.

438
00:24:07,039 --> 00:24:09,559
Does this mean the current drill

439
00:24:09,920 --> 00:24:11,640
is just a drill?

440
00:24:20,319 --> 00:24:21,160
How should I put it?

441
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:23,759
From a scientific perspective,

442
00:24:24,559 --> 00:24:26,319
without a hundred percent certainty of success,

443
00:24:26,519 --> 00:24:27,359
it's better not to fight.

444
00:24:31,279 --> 00:24:34,319
Your intel is like a box of matches.

445
00:24:35,519 --> 00:24:37,000
I'm going to use it to light a pack

446
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:38,640
of wet explosives.

447
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:40,319
If we guess right, everything will be fine.

448
00:24:40,759 --> 00:24:42,200
But if we guess wrong,

449
00:24:43,359 --> 00:24:44,880
it will ignite a war.

450
00:24:44,880 --> 00:24:46,759
Scientific data is absolute.

451
00:24:46,759 --> 00:24:49,160
But many wars in this world happen by chance.

452
00:24:58,759 --> 00:24:59,680
What do you mean?

453
00:25:03,319 --> 00:25:04,640
I don't want a war.

454
00:25:06,559 --> 00:25:08,000
I don't think you do either.

455
00:25:09,880 --> 00:25:11,279
At least the two of us,

456
00:25:11,680 --> 00:25:12,960
neither of us wants

457
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:16,720
what falls on this lake to be

458
00:25:16,759 --> 00:25:18,000
a missile instead of leaves.

459
00:25:22,160 --> 00:25:23,200
Broadly speaking,

460
00:25:23,759 --> 00:25:25,119
on behalf of the common people,

461
00:25:25,599 --> 00:25:26,799
and on a personal level,

462
00:25:28,240 --> 00:25:29,559
on behalf of my family,

463
00:25:31,480 --> 00:25:33,240
my old mother, my wife,

464
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:34,799
and my dog at home,

465
00:25:37,200 --> 00:25:38,160
I thank you.

466
00:25:43,640 --> 00:25:44,799
Please, please, please.

467
00:25:44,799 --> 00:25:45,799
Get up.

468
00:25:49,200 --> 00:25:50,160
You in person

469
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:53,559
are quite different

470
00:25:53,559 --> 00:25:55,000
from the man I imagined.

471
00:25:58,559 --> 00:25:59,839
I'm too big of a target.

472
00:26:00,359 --> 00:26:01,559
Next time we meet,

473
00:26:02,119 --> 00:26:03,720
I might find a runner

474
00:26:04,759 --> 00:26:06,359
to go back and forth between us.

475
00:26:07,319 --> 00:26:08,279
What kind of person is he?

476
00:26:08,599 --> 00:26:10,000
Someone you can trust.

477
00:26:10,519 --> 00:26:11,920
Someone you don't need direct contact with.

478
00:26:11,920 --> 00:26:15,079
This person will assist and protect you.

479
00:26:15,599 --> 00:26:16,799
Whenever you need him,

480
00:26:17,079 --> 00:26:18,079
he will appear.

481
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:23,880
This

482
00:26:24,240 --> 00:26:26,039
is your salary for three months.

483
00:26:27,640 --> 00:26:30,119
I've signed for it on your behalf.

484
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:46,400
Top Secret intelligence.

485
00:26:46,680 --> 00:26:48,039
Mobilize all resources

486
00:26:48,039 --> 00:26:49,039
to verify it immediately.

487
00:26:57,200 --> 00:26:59,079
One, two, three, four!

488
00:26:59,279 --> 00:27:01,200
One, two, three, four!

489
00:27:25,640 --> 00:27:26,440
Understood.

490
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:28,640
This is for you.

491
00:27:47,680 --> 00:27:49,240
I'm the best in the world.

492
00:27:49,440 --> 00:27:51,119
No one can outdrink me.

493
00:27:51,559 --> 00:27:52,079
Really.

494
00:27:52,559 --> 00:27:53,920
I totally don't...

495
00:27:54,400 --> 00:27:55,200
To be honest with you,

496
00:27:55,519 --> 00:27:56,200
before this,

497
00:27:56,319 --> 00:27:58,000
Xiao Lu didn't believe me either.

498
00:27:58,519 --> 00:27:59,640
I drank him under the table,

499
00:27:59,640 --> 00:28:01,920
he passed out right there.

500
00:28:01,920 --> 00:28:03,759
Alright, you did great today.

501
00:28:04,440 --> 00:28:05,000
I've been...

502
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:05,920
You really can hold your liquor.

503
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:07,039
drinking since I was a kid.

504
00:28:07,160 --> 00:28:08,039
Don't you doubt it.

505
00:28:08,200 --> 00:28:10,039
When I was little, my grandma

506
00:28:10,279 --> 00:28:12,039
would dip a chopstick in it

507
00:28:12,200 --> 00:28:13,880
and put it right in my mouth.

508
00:28:14,119 --> 00:28:15,079
"Have a taste."

509
00:28:15,200 --> 00:28:16,799
"Is it good?"

510
00:28:17,200 --> 00:28:18,519
It's always been like that.

511
00:28:18,519 --> 00:28:20,000
Do you know where the room is?

512
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:20,519
Here.

513
00:28:20,519 --> 00:28:21,319
This way.

514
00:28:21,880 --> 00:28:22,480
Here.

515
00:28:22,480 --> 00:28:23,640
Drinking since childhood...

516
00:28:25,319 --> 00:28:26,079
Slow down.

517
00:28:26,079 --> 00:28:26,880
Excuse me.

518
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:28,480
I got it.

519
00:28:34,519 --> 00:28:36,119
After you, Boss.

520
00:28:40,680 --> 00:28:41,400
Boss.

521
00:28:42,200 --> 00:28:43,079
Did you know?

522
00:28:43,559 --> 00:28:44,279
This time,

523
00:28:44,799 --> 00:28:47,119
Even the exhibition director's card,

524
00:28:47,119 --> 00:28:48,640
I managed to get it.

525
00:28:48,839 --> 00:28:50,680
Let me show you.

526
00:28:50,680 --> 00:28:51,240
Here.

527
00:28:52,519 --> 00:28:52,960
This...

528
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:54,400
is from Beijing.

529
00:28:54,400 --> 00:28:55,240
I've got a whole stack of them.

530
00:28:55,480 --> 00:28:57,279
This one is...

531
00:28:58,240 --> 00:28:59,240
from within the province.

532
00:29:00,240 --> 00:29:02,519
This one is from Xiamen.

533
00:29:02,519 --> 00:29:04,000
I heard on the radio a few days ago,

534
00:29:05,079 --> 00:29:06,839
someone publicly stated in the US,

535
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:09,200
talking about "Two Chinas."

536
00:29:10,480 --> 00:29:11,640
Weren't we aiming for peace?

537
00:29:12,240 --> 00:29:13,240
He wants Taiwan independence!

538
00:29:13,440 --> 00:29:14,279
Did you know that?

539
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:17,000
I'm on my own anyway, so it doesn't matter.

540
00:29:18,079 --> 00:29:19,519
But with your big family,

541
00:29:19,759 --> 00:29:21,000
do you still dare to go to Beijing?

542
00:29:21,319 --> 00:29:22,519
What makes a politician?

543
00:29:23,559 --> 00:29:26,000
They say what people want to hear,

544
00:29:26,920 --> 00:29:29,440
and spin lies to fit the occasion.

545
00:29:29,799 --> 00:29:31,640
Otherwise, why travel all that way?

546
00:29:33,279 --> 00:29:35,519
He publicly supported reunification before.

547
00:29:35,519 --> 00:29:37,000
He won't really push for independence.

548
00:29:38,079 --> 00:29:39,200
It's just noise.

549
00:29:39,920 --> 00:29:41,559
Just do your own job.

550
00:29:41,880 --> 00:29:43,200
Don't overthink the rest.

551
00:29:44,759 --> 00:29:45,640
I'm not afraid.

552
00:29:46,839 --> 00:29:47,920
What are you afraid of?

553
00:29:49,319 --> 00:29:52,519
And there's Yang Chunyang, Liu Chunyang...

554
00:29:52,640 --> 00:29:54,599
Also from Shenzhen.

555
00:29:54,599 --> 00:29:55,279
This one...

556
00:29:56,960 --> 00:29:58,319
I kind of forgot.

557
00:29:58,319 --> 00:29:59,920
Why aren't you saying anything?

558
00:30:00,440 --> 00:30:03,279
Are you a little worried?

559
00:30:04,200 --> 00:30:06,119
Boss, where are we...

560
00:30:06,119 --> 00:30:07,839
Where are we going tomorrow?

561
00:30:09,279 --> 00:30:10,079
We're heading back tomorrow.

562
00:30:10,400 --> 00:30:11,720
We're heading back tomorrow?

563
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:13,640
We still have a few days.

564
00:30:20,079 --> 00:30:21,599
Are you alright?

565
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:49,519
I'm going to the restroom.

566
00:31:59,000 --> 00:31:59,880
Young man,

567
00:31:59,880 --> 00:32:00,839
may I ask you something?

568
00:32:00,839 --> 00:32:02,960
Do you know where the luggage storage is?

569
00:32:03,359 --> 00:32:05,200
I don't know. Probably outside.

570
00:32:06,920 --> 00:32:07,599
Thanks.

571
00:32:14,079 --> 00:32:15,359
Ladies and gentlemen,

572
00:32:15,559 --> 00:32:17,519
I am the chief purser for this flight.

573
00:32:17,839 --> 00:32:20,519
Our aircraft has reached cruising altitude.

574
00:32:20,960 --> 00:32:23,400
The captain has turned off the seatbelt sign.

575
00:32:23,799 --> 00:32:25,400
However, while seated,

576
00:32:25,400 --> 00:32:27,839
we still recommend keeping your seatbelt fastened.

577
00:32:28,119 --> 00:32:29,599
Ladies and gentlemen,

578
00:32:30,160 --> 00:32:32,680
I am the chief purser for this flight.

579
00:32:33,119 --> 00:32:36,279
Our aircraft has reached cruising altitude.

580
00:32:49,119 --> 00:32:49,880
Hello.

581
00:32:50,079 --> 00:32:51,519
May I borrow your newspaper?

582
00:32:53,519 --> 00:32:54,240
Here you go.

583
00:32:54,680 --> 00:32:55,720
Thank you.

584
00:32:55,720 --> 00:32:57,359
They were all gone when I tried to get one.

585
00:32:57,880 --> 00:32:58,519
You're welcome.

586
00:34:38,960 --> 00:34:39,920
Over a decade ago,

587
00:34:39,920 --> 00:34:41,079
on the mainland,

588
00:34:41,079 --> 00:34:43,280
those who could pick up broadcasts from Taiwan, China,

589
00:34:43,280 --> 00:34:45,480
would occasionally hear Taiwan, China

590
00:34:45,480 --> 00:34:47,360
sending coded messages to their sleeper agents.

591
00:34:47,519 --> 00:34:48,559
These coded messages

592
00:34:49,079 --> 00:34:51,800
usually used four-character codes

593
00:34:51,800 --> 00:34:53,159
to transmit orders.

594
00:34:53,440 --> 00:34:56,480
And later, spies from Taiwan, China on the mainland

595
00:34:56,480 --> 00:34:58,360
will continue to receive such coded messages.

596
00:35:13,239 --> 00:35:14,599
I heard you went home with heatstroke.

597
00:35:14,599 --> 00:35:15,159
How are you feeling?

598
00:35:15,960 --> 00:35:17,000
It's easy to handle as long as there's medicine.

599
00:35:17,239 --> 00:35:18,119
Just one step away.

600
00:35:18,920 --> 00:35:19,880
What are you talking about?

601
00:35:20,079 --> 00:35:21,480
Didn't you ask me to find evidence?

602
00:35:22,039 --> 00:35:22,800
I'll have it very soon.

603
00:36:31,880 --> 00:36:33,360
Brother Qi just went back to the office.

604
00:36:33,360 --> 00:36:34,800
That's how I found out you were back.

605
00:36:36,239 --> 00:36:38,039
I was just passing by your place after work.

606
00:36:38,360 --> 00:36:39,440
If you haven't had dinner yet,

607
00:36:40,119 --> 00:36:40,840
let's grab a bite.

608
00:36:43,440 --> 00:36:45,599
Is... is something the matter?

609
00:36:46,559 --> 00:36:48,039
I might be getting transferred soon.

610
00:36:55,559 --> 00:36:56,480
Well?

611
00:37:00,679 --> 00:37:02,039
Even if he's totally drunk,

612
00:37:02,039 --> 00:37:03,039
or incredibly scheming,

613
00:37:03,039 --> 00:37:04,320
or a massive fraud,

614
00:37:04,320 --> 00:37:05,639
we got the money anyway.

615
00:37:05,639 --> 00:37:06,639
What are you afraid of?

616
00:37:07,079 --> 00:37:09,239
If I knew he'd pay us in advance,

617
00:37:09,239 --> 00:37:10,840
I should've asked for two more months.

618
00:37:11,039 --> 00:37:11,920
He wants to hire you,

619
00:37:11,920 --> 00:37:12,840
and he wants to hire me too.

620
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:13,920
But why?

621
00:37:16,639 --> 00:37:17,400
Think about it.

622
00:37:17,960 --> 00:37:19,079
I'm practically a nobody.

623
00:37:19,280 --> 00:37:20,440
His watch was so expensive,

624
00:37:20,440 --> 00:37:21,519
yet he didn't call the police.

625
00:37:22,000 --> 00:37:23,599
He paid to get it back himself.

626
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:25,320
He's obviously playing a game.

627
00:37:25,440 --> 00:37:26,679
What game?

628
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:28,800
People don't do things for no reason.

629
00:37:28,960 --> 00:37:30,239
Does he just want my driving skills?

630
00:37:30,760 --> 00:37:31,840
Or your secretarial skills?

631
00:37:33,079 --> 00:37:34,039
What do you mean?

632
00:37:34,199 --> 00:37:34,800
Just say what you mean.

633
00:37:34,800 --> 00:37:36,000
Do I even need to spell it out?

634
00:37:36,119 --> 00:37:37,840
I already know what he's up to.

635
00:37:38,719 --> 00:37:40,400
Don't play dumb.

636
00:37:48,679 --> 00:37:50,400
I recognize that Taiwanese businessman.

637
00:37:50,840 --> 00:37:52,400
He gave me a tip before.

638
00:37:52,599 --> 00:37:55,039
Bro, I can tell you're a big boss.

639
00:37:56,199 --> 00:37:57,719
You look great.

640
00:37:57,920 --> 00:38:00,039
The kind who definitely makes a fortune every year.

641
00:38:00,679 --> 00:38:02,920
Bro, if you could look out for me,

642
00:38:03,119 --> 00:38:04,440
and give me some money for smokes,

643
00:38:04,559 --> 00:38:06,039
you'll make another fortune by the end of the year.

644
00:38:08,320 --> 00:38:10,119
The thing is, I can't pee with you doing this.

645
00:38:10,679 --> 00:38:11,639
Others might not recognize you,

646
00:38:11,639 --> 00:38:12,599
but I do.

647
00:38:12,599 --> 00:38:14,400
Being a big boss is tough.

648
00:38:17,239 --> 00:38:18,440
I just started peeing,

649
00:38:18,639 --> 00:38:19,400
and when you grabbed me,

650
00:38:19,559 --> 00:38:20,920
I peed on my shoe.

651
00:38:21,280 --> 00:38:21,519
I'm sorry.

652
00:38:21,519 --> 00:38:22,639
These shoes are very expensive.

653
00:38:22,639 --> 00:38:24,119
A friend brought them from the US to Taipei,

654
00:38:24,119 --> 00:38:25,519
and I wore them from Taipei to here.

655
00:38:25,559 --> 00:38:26,920
You can't even buy them with money.

656
00:38:27,039 --> 00:38:27,960
They cost a few thousand.

657
00:38:28,119 --> 00:38:28,920
What are you doing?

658
00:38:28,920 --> 00:38:29,639
I'm sorry, boss.

659
00:38:29,639 --> 00:38:30,360
I'm sorry, my mistake.

660
00:38:30,360 --> 00:38:31,159
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

661
00:38:31,159 --> 00:38:32,159
Well, aren't you going to wipe them?

662
00:38:38,760 --> 00:38:39,440
Brother,

663
00:38:40,320 --> 00:38:41,400
you need shoe polish.

664
00:38:41,400 --> 00:38:42,559
Wiping them like that won't work.

665
00:38:42,760 --> 00:38:44,039
This is genuine leather.

666
00:38:44,039 --> 00:38:45,119
Do you think you're scrubbing a toilet?

667
00:38:45,119 --> 00:38:45,599
I'll go buy some right now.

668
00:38:45,599 --> 00:38:46,199
I'll be quick, very quick.

669
00:38:46,199 --> 00:38:47,000
Wait a minute.

670
00:38:54,320 --> 00:38:54,639
No need, no need.

671
00:38:54,639 --> 00:38:55,639
I have some, boss.

672
00:38:58,000 --> 00:38:59,119
Just kidding.

673
00:38:59,440 --> 00:39:00,480
Did I scare you?

674
00:39:03,519 --> 00:39:04,840
He's an old fox.

675
00:39:05,199 --> 00:39:06,159
He's rich,

676
00:39:06,440 --> 00:39:07,719
and lives all by himself.

677
00:39:07,840 --> 00:39:09,159
Don't you think he has his own schemes?

678
00:39:17,400 --> 00:39:18,599
I wasn't talking about you.

679
00:39:19,679 --> 00:39:20,719
I was talking about him.

680
00:39:21,159 --> 00:39:23,199
What if he has his own ideas?

681
00:39:25,119 --> 00:39:27,639
You're just afraid he'll steal me away.

682
00:39:27,719 --> 00:39:28,559
If you cared about me,

683
00:39:28,559 --> 00:39:29,800
you should just say so.

684
00:39:29,800 --> 00:39:30,760
If you don't care,

685
00:39:30,760 --> 00:39:32,239
we'll see if I ever talk to you again.

686
00:39:32,760 --> 00:39:34,440
He wants to use my aunt's connections

687
00:39:34,440 --> 00:39:35,559
to do business in military assets.

688
00:39:35,639 --> 00:39:37,000
What military business?

689
00:39:37,360 --> 00:39:39,119
That's obviously a roundabout scheme.

690
00:39:39,400 --> 00:39:41,039
He never had good intentions to begin with.

691
00:39:44,440 --> 00:39:45,960
My home is on Xiangyang Street.

692
00:39:47,039 --> 00:39:49,199
Two blocks west of here,

693
00:39:49,320 --> 00:39:50,440
just around the corner.

694
00:39:51,039 --> 00:39:52,599
If Huadong hadn't told me you lived here,

695
00:39:52,599 --> 00:39:54,559
I wouldn't have known I pass your house every day.

696
00:39:54,760 --> 00:39:56,559
Huadong said he's looking to rent too.

697
00:39:56,800 --> 00:39:58,199
He wants to be closer to work.

698
00:39:58,440 --> 00:40:00,519
He might be looking around here too.

699
00:40:01,760 --> 00:40:02,559
Maybe.

700
00:40:05,440 --> 00:40:07,679
Two days in Beijing and your accent changed.

701
00:40:09,400 --> 00:40:11,159
How was it? Was Beijing fun?

702
00:40:14,920 --> 00:40:16,320
Why do you want to leave?

703
00:40:16,719 --> 00:40:18,320
Is it your own choice,

704
00:40:18,440 --> 00:40:19,679
or orders from above?

705
00:40:20,199 --> 00:40:21,840
Boss, two more skewers of this.

706
00:40:22,360 --> 00:40:22,760
Okay, coming right up.

707
00:40:22,760 --> 00:40:24,519
I don't know why I'm always hungry lately.

708
00:40:29,400 --> 00:40:31,239
Working overtime makes you hungry easily.

709
00:40:31,559 --> 00:40:33,039
Have you guys been busy lately?

710
00:40:34,159 --> 00:40:35,519
Didn't you ask me to find evidence?

711
00:40:36,159 --> 00:40:38,039
Almost. I can't say much right now.

712
00:40:38,320 --> 00:40:39,239
But I'm sure

713
00:40:39,360 --> 00:40:40,559
there's definitely something wrong with him.

714
00:40:41,039 --> 00:40:41,679
All right.

715
00:40:41,840 --> 00:40:43,760
Let's see who's faster, you or me.

716
00:40:47,840 --> 00:40:49,559
I might go into surveillance.

717
00:40:49,760 --> 00:40:50,639
Full-time.

718
00:40:52,679 --> 00:40:54,239
Wouldn't that mean joining a task force?

719
00:40:54,559 --> 00:40:55,320
Which unit?

720
00:40:55,480 --> 00:40:56,679
Is it still in our division?

721
00:40:59,599 --> 00:41:00,639
After working all day,

722
00:41:01,119 --> 00:41:02,920
I don't want to say a single word I'm allowed to,

723
00:41:03,199 --> 00:41:04,599
and I can't say what I actually want to.

724
00:41:05,039 --> 00:41:06,119
Isn't that annoying?

725
00:41:08,920 --> 00:41:10,679
That doesn't suit your personality.

726
00:41:11,079 --> 00:41:12,159
I'm actually pretty used to it.

727
00:41:12,440 --> 00:41:14,159
Living like I'm mute and deaf.

728
00:41:14,599 --> 00:41:16,400
To be honest, working a job like this,

729
00:41:17,000 --> 00:41:17,960
don't you get sick of it?

730
00:41:20,719 --> 00:41:21,760
Growing up,

731
00:41:22,079 --> 00:41:23,920
nobody ever asked me what I wanted to do,

732
00:41:23,920 --> 00:41:24,800
or what I could do.

733
00:41:24,800 --> 00:41:26,119
My dad is a primary school teacher.

734
00:41:26,320 --> 00:41:27,800
He thought being a teacher was good.

735
00:41:27,800 --> 00:41:29,000
My mom is a nurse.

736
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:30,320
She thought being a doctor was good.

737
00:41:30,679 --> 00:41:32,400
But actually, I didn't like either.

738
00:41:32,679 --> 00:41:34,119
I just wanted to be a soldier.

739
00:41:35,639 --> 00:41:36,679
But after I enlisted,

740
00:41:36,960 --> 00:41:37,800
I realized

741
00:41:38,039 --> 00:41:39,920
I wasn't suited to be a soldier at all.

742
00:41:40,320 --> 00:41:41,760
Who said you weren't suited for it?

743
00:41:41,920 --> 00:41:44,159
Squad leader, platoon leader, company commander...

744
00:41:44,760 --> 00:41:45,719
They all said so.

745
00:41:46,440 --> 00:41:47,800
But the more they said it,

746
00:41:47,800 --> 00:41:49,360
the more I wanted to prove myself.

747
00:41:49,360 --> 00:41:50,719
Later, I went to study military medicine.

748
00:41:51,199 --> 00:41:52,440
I just wanted to stay

749
00:41:52,440 --> 00:41:53,639
and prove them wrong to the end.

750
00:41:56,840 --> 00:41:58,000
And now?

751
00:41:58,000 --> 00:41:59,480
What do you think you're suited for?

752
00:42:00,239 --> 00:42:01,760
Intelligence or recon?

753
00:42:03,320 --> 00:42:04,639
Being the spear or the shield?

754
00:42:07,599 --> 00:42:09,199
Wasn't I the one asking the questions?

755
00:42:09,199 --> 00:42:10,719
How come you're asking me now?

756
00:42:12,559 --> 00:42:13,920
You really shouldn't leave.

757
00:42:14,159 --> 00:42:16,280
You're the most talented among all of us.

758
00:42:16,280 --> 00:42:17,199
Brother Qi said so.

759
00:42:17,519 --> 00:42:18,360
What about you?

760
00:42:18,360 --> 00:42:19,800
What do you think I'm most suited for?

761
00:42:20,320 --> 00:42:22,159
I think you're suited for anything.

762
00:42:22,639 --> 00:42:24,760
If I had to pick a partner for surveillance,

763
00:42:24,760 --> 00:42:25,760
I'd definitely pick you.

764
00:42:26,599 --> 00:42:27,639
I wouldn't do it.

765
00:42:27,639 --> 00:42:28,920
You're too tight-lipped.

766
00:42:28,920 --> 00:42:29,519
You went to Beijing,

767
00:42:29,519 --> 00:42:31,159
and didn't even say if the roast duck was good.

768
00:42:31,760 --> 00:42:33,320
If I partnered with you for surveillance,

769
00:42:33,320 --> 00:42:34,519
I'd be bored to death.

770
00:42:36,639 --> 00:42:37,679
Actually,

771
00:42:38,920 --> 00:42:40,519
once you get to know me,

772
00:42:40,760 --> 00:42:42,840
I can be quite talkative.

773
00:42:42,840 --> 00:42:44,719
I'm just afraid you'll find me too chatty.

774
00:42:47,000 --> 00:42:48,519
You really are a strange person.

775
00:42:49,639 --> 00:42:50,719
What do you mean?

776
00:42:53,599 --> 00:42:54,360
You're hard to read.

777
00:42:55,400 --> 00:42:56,559
I can't figure you out at all.

778
00:43:08,480 --> 00:43:09,199
I am Wang Kai,

779
00:43:09,480 --> 00:43:11,000
inviting you to watch the drama

780
00:43:11,239 --> 00:43:11,960
"Confrontation".

781
00:43:11,960 --> 00:43:13,159
Throwing intel around just like that...

782
00:43:13,239 --> 00:43:14,719
What happens to us if they blow their cover?

783
00:43:14,760 --> 00:43:15,599
If they're going to play their hand,

784
00:43:15,599 --> 00:43:16,320
then we'll arrest every single

785
00:43:16,480 --> 00:43:17,519
gambler at the table.

786
00:43:17,519 --> 00:43:18,280
Initiate ahead of schedule,

787
00:43:18,280 --> 00:43:19,559
Operation Spring Thunder No. 1.

788
00:43:19,559 --> 00:43:20,239
From now on,

789
00:43:20,239 --> 00:43:21,639
the target Ma Qi's team is watching

790
00:43:21,639 --> 00:43:22,880
will be wiretapped by Jin Lan.

791
00:43:23,119 --> 00:43:24,000
Officially open the case

792
00:43:24,000 --> 00:43:24,880
and place them under close surveillance.

793
00:43:24,880 --> 00:43:26,000
Your cover identity

794
00:43:26,000 --> 00:43:28,440
is a tour guide at Shenzhou Strait Travel Agency.
